    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Dorrian are delighted to present to the market this beautifully maintained three bedroom semi-detached bungalow, ideally\npositioned within a small and welcoming development of just 16 homes, only a two-minute walk from Kilcar Village. Bungalows of this size and quality are becoming increasingly difficult to find, particularly within such easy walking distance of local shops, services and village amenities. The property is therefore likely to appeal to downsizers, retired purchasers, first-time buyers or anyone seeking a comfortable and manageable home in a highly convenient setting. Remaining in the same ownership since it was originally built, the bungalow has been exceptionally well cared for and is presented in excellent condition throughout.\n\nThe accommodation is bright, practical and well proportioned, comprising three bedrooms together with comfortable living\nspace suited to modern everyday living. A further advantage is the property's larger-than-average site when compared with similar homes within the development. This provides generous outdoor space, greater privacy and excellent potential for gardening, seating or further landscaping. Combining careful long-term ownership, a peaceful residential setting and an\nexcellent village location, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a well-presented bungalow within easy walking distance of the\nheart of Kilcar."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance hall: - 4.5m x 2.0m\n- with ceramic tiled floor, composite uPVC door with frosted glass porthole and glass side panel, built-in cloakroom with clothe rails, fitted hotpress with copper tank and electric wallis water heater, 2 x centre lights.\n\nSitting Room: - 4.6m x 3.1m\n- with oak effect laminate floor, tiled fireplace with granite hearth, fitted solid fuel Stanley stove with wooden mantel over, roller blinds, coaxial TV points, centre light.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: - 3.7m x 2.4m\n- with ceramic tiled floor, laminate wall and base units, black marble effect worktops, one and a half sink with swan neck tap, Creda electric oven, Belling (4) x ring hotplate with extractor canopy over, slot-in Zanussi fridge/freezer, casual dining area with clear glass door out to backyard, finnish and blinds, chrome (4) x ring centre light, analogue time clock.\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.6m x 3.5m\n- with oak effect laminate floor, roller blinds, centre light.\n\nBedroom 2: - 3.3m x 3.3m\nwith oak effect laminate floor, roller blinds, centre light.\n\nBedroom 3: - 2.8m x 2.3m\nwith oak effect laminate floor, roller blinds, centre light.\n\nBathroom: - 2.3 x 1.7m\n- with modern sanitary ware in white comprising of a dual flush w.c, pedestal wash hand basin with mirror and shaver light over, bath with chrome mixer taps and shower cradle, half tiled wall, fully tiled around bath, ceramic tiled floor, concealed centre light.\n\nStore: - 2.4m x 1.7m\n- with power supply and lighting, plumber for washing machine.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Additional Features:</li><li> Beautifully maintained three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow extending to c. 74.9 sq.m in area.</li><li> Located within a small, welcoming development of only 16 homes.</li><li> Approximately a two-minute walk from Kilcar Village and local amenities.</li><li> Rare opportunity to acquire a manageable bungalow in a convenient village setting.</li><li> Same ownership since originally constructed.</li><li> Oil fired central heaing.</li><li> uPVC windows and doors throughout.</li><li> Exceptionally well cared for and presented in excellent condition throughout.</li><li> Bright, practical and well-proportioned accommodation.</li><li> Comfortable sitting room with solid-fuel Stanley stove.</li><li> Fitted kitchen and dining area with direct access to the rear garden.</li><li> Three well-sized bedrooms with oak-effect laminate flooring.</li><li> Private driveway with ample parking and gated entrance to rear.</li><li> Modern bathroom with bath and shower fitting.</li><li> Larger-than-average site compared with similar homes in the development.</li><li> Generous outdoor space offering added privacy finished in sandstone paving and decorative gravel.</li><li> Ideally suited to downsizers, retired purchasers, first-time buyers or those seeking a low-maintenance home.</li><li> Viewings by prior arrangement with DNG Dorrian on 074 97 31291.</ul>"
      },
